    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should strongly consider taking this offer.** \n\nSecuring a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** alongside a $1.08M equity grant and a base match at $240,000 puts this well into the top tier for a Google L6 Product Manager in the Bay Area.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Updated Numbers\n\nUnder Google\u2019s standard front-loaded vesting schedule (33% / 33% / 22% / 12%):\n\n| Year | Base Salary | Target Bonus (20%) | Sign-On Bonus | GSU Vesting | **Total Compensation** | **Delta vs. Meta (~$526k)** |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $200,000 | $356,400 | **~$844,400** | **+$318,400 (+60%)** |\n| **Year 2** | $240,000 | $48,000 | \u2014 | $356,400 | **~$644,400** | **+$118,400 (+22%)** |\n| **Year 3** | $240,000 | $48,000 | \u2014 | $237,600 | **~$525,600\\*** | At parity (before refreshes) |\n| **Year 4** | $240,000 | $48,000 | \u2014 | $129,600 | **~$417,600\\*** | Refreshes needed |\n\n*\\*Excludes annual equity refreshes, merit increases, and stock appreciation.*\n\n* **2-Year Realized Comp:** You will make **~$1.49M in your first 24 months** (versus ~$1.05M at Meta) \u2014 an extra **~$440,000+** in gross earnings over two years.\n* **4-Year Total Value:** Guaranteed package value of **$2.43M** (an average of **~$608,000/year** pre-refreshes).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This is a Big Win\n\n1. **Cash De-risks Your Transition:** Converting your $200k in unvested Meta RSUs into guaranteed cash upfront eliminates market volatility risk for that chunk of your compensation.\n2. **Year 1\u20132 Earning Power:** Earning ~$844k in Year 1 and ~$644k in Year 2 gives you immediate upside that Meta is unlikely to match without an extraordinary off-cycle retention package.\n3. **Resume / Market Value:** Having both Meta (IC6) and Google (L6) on your resume gives you elite product leadership pedigree across two different operating cultures.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Details to Confirm Before Signing\n\nReview the fine print on these standard terms:\n\n* **Sign-On Clawback Terms:** Confirm whether the $200,000 is paid in your first paycheck and whether the clawback is a standard 12-month prorated repayment if you leave voluntarily.\n* **Vesting Schedule & Cadence:** Confirm the exact vesting split (typically 33/33/22/12) and whether vests occur monthly or quarterly after the initial cliff.\n* **Bonus Proration:** Check how your Year 1 performance bonus will be prorated based on your start date.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Verdict\n\nThey met your ask on the base salary and covered your walking-away equity dollar-for-dollar in cash. You negotiated high leverage into maximum value. Unless you have deep non-monetary reservations about the specific Google team or scope, **accept the offer.**",
